{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run/agent-source && grep -n \\\"func (p \\\\*pendingReadIndex) dropped\\\" -A 12 request.go && sed -n 1662,1696p internal/raft/raft.go\"","aggregated_output":"892:func (p *pendingReadIndex) dropped(system pb.SystemCtx) {\n893-\tp.mu.Lock()\n894-\tdefer p.mu.Unlock()\n895-\tif p.stopped {\n896-\t\treturn\n897-\t}\n898-\tif rb, ok := p.batches[system]; ok {\n899-\t\tfor _, req := range rb.requests {\n900-\t\t\tif req != nil {\n901-\t\t\t\treq.dropped()\n902-\t\t\t}\n903-\t\t}\n904-\t\tdelete(p.batches, system)\nfunc (r *raft) handleLeaderReadIndex(m pb.Message) {\n\tr.mustBeLeader()\n\tctx := pb.SystemCtx{\n\t\tHigh: m.HintHigh,\n\t\tLow:  m.Hint,\n\t}\n\tif _, wok := r.witnesses[m.From]; wok {\n\t\tplog.Errorf(\"%s dropped ReadIndex, witness node %d\", r.describe(), m.From)\n\t} else if !r.isSingleNodeQuorum() {\n\t\tif !r.hasCommittedEntryAtCurrentTerm() {\n\t\t\t// leader doesn't know the commit value of the cluster\n\t\t\t// see raft thesis section 6.4, this is the first step of the ReadIndex\n\t\t\t// protocol.\n\t\t\tplog.Warningf(\"%s dropped ReadIndex, not ready\", r.describe())\n\t\t\tr.reportDroppedReadIndex(m)\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.readIndex.addRequest(r.log.committed, ctx, m.From)\n\t\tr.broadcastHeartbeatMessageWithHint(ctx)\n\t} else {\n\t\tr.addReadyToRead(r.log.committed, ctx)\n\t\t_, ook := r.observers[m.From]\n\t\tif m.From != r.nodeID && ook {\n\t\t\tr.send(pb.Message{\n\t\t\t\tTo:       m.From,\n\t\t\t\tType:     pb.ReadIndexResp,\n\t\t\t\tLogIndex: r.log.committed,\n\t\t\t\tHint:     m.Hint,\n\t\t\t\tHintHigh: m.HintHigh,\n\t\t\t\tCommit:   m.Commit,\n\t\t\t})\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nout={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Check whether a ReadIndex rejected at the leader is reported back to a remote requester. handleLeaderReadIndex drops the request with reportDroppedReadIndex when the leader has no committed entry in its current term, and that call appends the forwarded message's context to the leader's own droppedReadIndexes list; node.processDroppedReadIndexes then feeds those contexts to the leader's pendingReadIndex.dropped, which only completes batches whose key matches. A follower-forwarded read has no batch on the leader, so the drop is consumed locally and the originating node is never told; its client waits for the caller deadline instead of observing ErrClusterNotReady. This is a bounded completion gap distinct from the context substitution: the trigger is a freshly elected leader before its no-op commits, and the cause is a drop notification addressed to the wrong node.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"leader-readindex-drop-path\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"internal/raft/raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1662,\\\"end_line\\\":1696,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"report-dropped-readindex\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"internal/raft/raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":2064,\\\"end_line\\\":2072,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"node-process-dropped-readindexes\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"node.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1021,\\\"end_line\\\":1025,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"pending-read-dropped\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"request.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":892,\\\"end_line\\\":904,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[\n  {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@readindex-drop-not-propagated\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"When a leader rejects a follower-forwarded ReadIndex because it has no committed entry in its current term, does the originating node learn that the request was dropped, or does its pending read wait for the caller deadline?\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"reportDroppedReadIndex records the forwarded context in the leader's own update, and pendingReadIndex.dropped only completes batches keyed by that context on the leader, so a remote requester is never notified and its read waits for its deadline.\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"leader-readindex-drop-path\\\",\\\"report-dropped-readindex\\\",\\\"node-process-dropped-readindexes\\\",\\\"pending-read-dropped\\\"]}\n ],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@readindex-drop-not-propagated\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"handleLeaderReadIndex rejects a follower-forwarded ReadIndex when the leader has no committed entry in its current term and calls reportDroppedReadIndex, which appends the forwarded message's SystemCtx to the leader's droppedReadIndexes list without sending anything to the requester. node.processDroppedReadIndexes passes each of those contexts to pendingReadIndex.dropped, which completes only requests in a batch keyed by that same context, so the leader has nothing to complete and the originating node's batch is untouched.\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":\\\"The leader is not a single-node quorum, has no committed entry in its current term, and receives a ReadIndex forwarded by a follower or observer.\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"leader-readindex-drop-path\\\",\\\"report-dropped-readindex\\\",\\\"node-process-dropped-readindexes\\\",\\\"pending-read-dropped\\\"]}\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@readindex-drop-not-propagated\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"leader-readindex-drop-path\\\",\\\"report-dropped-readindex\\\",\\\"node-process-dropped-readindexes\\\",\\\"pending-read-dropped\\\"],\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"A follower-forwarded ReadIndex that the leader rejects for lack of a current-term committed entry is dropped silently with respect to the requester. The leader records the forwarded context in its own update, and the local drop handler only completes batches keyed by that context, which exist on the originating node rather than on the leader. The requester therefore keeps its pending batch at index zero until its own timeout, so the caller sees ErrTimeout at its deadline rather than the ErrClusterNotReady that the dropped path produces for a locally admitted read. The trigger is legal and recurrent: every newly elected leader passes through a window before its current-term no-op commits during which handleLeaderReadIndex takes the not-ready branch, and followers forward their reads into it. This is a bounded client-completion gap, not a safety issue; no stale read follows from it. The repair implied by the source is to report the dropped context back to the originating node, for example by answering the forwarded request with a drop indication that its pendingReadIndex consumes.\\\",\\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"@readindex-drop-not-propagated\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"A rejected forwarded read is recorded on the leader and never reported to the originating node.\\\"}],\\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The drop path only defers the read; the requester's own deadline still ends the wait, so no unbounded hang is established.\\\",\\\"The leader-side drop is visible in its own update and through the warning log, so an operator can observe that reads were dropped even though the requester cannot.\\\",\\\"A locally admitted read on a leader in the same state does receive ErrClusterNotReady through pendingReadIndex.dropped, which shows the notification mechanism exists and is simply not addressed to the remote requester.\\\"],\\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"This is a source-only account; no execution drives a follower-forwarded read into the not-ready branch and samples the caller endpoint.\\\",\\\"It does not measure how long the not-ready window lasts after an election, which depends on how quickly the new leader commits its no-op.\\\",\\\"The account covers the no-current-term-entry rejection; other rejection branches in handleLeaderReadIndex are not separately traced here.\\\"]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(out, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=2)\nopen('draft/update.json','a').write(\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance && .venv/bin/consensus-assurance validate --run runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
